Rule 1 (tensor shapes should be the same)
{v_1 : tensor, v_2 : tensor} |= ndim(v_1) = ndim(v_2) ∧ ∀i ∈ [0, ndim(v_1) - 1] : shape(v_1, i) = shape(v_2, i)
>>
Rule 2 (valid 2D transposed convolution)
{v_1 : tensor, v_2 : tensor, v_3 : int, v_4 : int} |= ndim(v_1) = 4 ∧ ndim(v_2) = 4 ∧ v_3 ≥ 1 ∧ v_4 ≥ 0 ∧ v_3 × (shape(v_1, 2) - 1) + shape(v_2, 2) - 2 × v_4 > 0 ∧ v_3 × (shape(v_1, 3) - 1) + shape(v_2, 3) - 2 × v_4 > 0
>>
Rule 3 (index tensor (v_2) should be within the range of input tensor)
{v_1 : tensor, v_2 : tensor} |= min(v_2) ≥ 0 ∧ ∀i ∈ [0, ndim(v_1) - 1] : max(v_2) ≤ shape(v_1, i) - 1
>>
Rule 4 (first dimension of a tensor matches second dimension of the other)
{v_1 : tensor, v_2 : tensor} |= ndim(v_1) ≥ 1 ∧ ndim(v_2) ≥ 2 ∧ shape(v_1, 0) = shape(v_2, 1)
>>
Rule 5 (tuple of ints used as kernel size must have length 2)
{v_1 : tuple(int)} |= v_1.len = 2 ∧ ∀i ∈ [0, 1] : v_1[i] > 0
>>
Rule 6 (tensor parameter should be valid for kaiser_window)
{v_1 : tensor} |= ndim(v_1) ≥ 1 ∧ shape(v_1, 0) ≥ 1 ∧ shape(v_1, 0) ≤ 1000000
>>
Rule 7 (int parameter should be valid for kaiser_window)
{v_1 : int} |= v_1 ≥ 1 ∧ v_1 ≤ 1000000
>>
Rule 8 (float parameter should be valid for kaiser_window)
{v_1 : float} |= v_1 ≥ 0.0 ∧ v_1 ≤ 1000000.0
>>
Rule 9 (bool parameter should be valid for kaiser_window)
{v_1 : bool} |= v_1 = True ∨ v_1 = False
